 When a dynamic object of a spell exists, it is the one that is drawn (its radius is the truth), so Blizzard shows one
 circle, not two.
 
+The chain circle is only shown while the spell is being cast (it needs the target of the cast, or failing that the
+caster's current target). The server decides the real jump distance and it is not in the client data, so `ChainRadius`
+is a best guess; for a spell where it is off, a row in the override file sets the right radius for that spell
+(`circle,dest,<radius>`: `dest` is the target unit when the spell has no ground point).
+
